  BiosDocHelp_Begin()
  BiosDocHelp_L("* This document concerns MSXes from 1. Note turboR was not released when this document was authored.")
  BiosDocHelp_L("")
  BiosDocHelp_L("2.2.5 Software Reset")
  BiosDocHelp_L("")
  BiosDocHelp_L("If you reset an MSX by jumping to 0 address (this is called a software reset) you might disable kanji ROM. Device enable function is the cause of this symptom.")
  BiosDocHelp_L("")
  BiosDocHelp_L("Device enable is a name of function to prevent bus conflict. For example, if you connect an external kanji ROM to a MSX equipped with internal kanji ROM, this means two devices are stuck into one I/O port, therefore causing conflicts between signals coming from these kanji ROMs, and in worst case, MSX itself will crush. To prevent this, F5H of I/O port is supplied as device enable function, and it works as follows.")
  BiosDocHelp_L("")
  BiosDocHelp_L("When you turn power of an MSX on, MSX assumes its internal kanji ROM as disconnected, and BIOS checks kanji ROM status. Since internal kanji ROM is disconnected, if MSX detects a kanji ROM presence, the detected kanji ROM should be an external one.")
  BiosDocHelp_L("")
  BiosDocHelp_L("If no external kanji ROM was found, MSX writes 1 to bit 0 of F5H I/O port and enables internal kanji ROM (refer to page 391 of MSX2 Technical Handbook - I don't know correspondent page no. in English version;). These procedures so far allow you to insert an external kanji ROM into an MSX with internal kanji ROM. RS-232C is supported by similar function too.")
  BiosDocHelp_L("")
  BiosDocHelp_L("But, if a program jumps to 0 address through commands like JP 0H (C3 00 00), MSX will go to the rountine to check kanji ROM status, while assuming internal kanji ROM is connected. When this happens, MSX thinks its internal kanji ROM as external one, and disconnects it. There is no problem if an MSX goes to the routine to check external device at the time of power on and pressing a reset button, but if you want to let a program to reset, in another word, if you want to jump to 00H, you must perfrom some preventive measure. Practical method is as follows;")
  BiosDocHelp_L("")
  BiosDocHelp_L("* If you want to let a software to reset, execute the following.")
  BiosDocHelp_L("")
  BiosDocHelp_L("LD   A,00H")
  BiosDocHelp_L("OUT (F5H),A")
  BiosDocHelp_L("JP  0H")
  BiosDocHelp_L("")
  BiosDocHelp_L("Basically, as MSX2 Technical Handbook insists, users are forbidden to read or write F5H of I/O, so this is not a very appreciated method, but there are no other means to abort the problem. Note even this procedure cannot solve misguided execution; in that case, it means the I/O F5H of your MSX operates dissimilar to other MSXes. (This is possible to happen, since direct accesses to F5H are not in MSX developer's mind)")
  BiosDocHelp_L("")
  BiosDocHelp_L("Note, with MSX2+, external devices are always disconnected by writing 0 into F5H I/O, so you can safely write 0.")
  BiosDocHelp_L("")
  BiosDocHelp_L("Also, since MSX2+, you can check reset status. Use added BIOS to do so.")
  BiosDocHelp_L("")
  BiosDocHelp_L("* If you want to check reset status with MSX2+, do as follows.")
  BiosDocHelp_L("")
  BiosDocHelp_L("CALL 017AH")
  BiosDocHelp_L("")
  BiosDocHelp_L("After doing this, if bit 7 of returned A register is standing, you can learn that MSX was restarted by JP 0H reset (software reset). If the bit 7 is not standing, it means an MSX was resetted by hardware reset. I guess this function was added because if software cannot detect between hardware reset and software reset, many troubles are likely to happen. In fact, a hardware to check reset is added to F4H of I/O, and inside of the BIOS here reads and write the F4H port.")
  BiosDocHelp_L("")
  BiosDocHelp_L("To safely use this function, you must let a software which is going to execute software reset to write a value. Use a BIOS which was newly implemented since MSX2+, too.")
  BiosDocHelp_L("")
  BiosDocHelp_L("* If you want to reset an MSX2+, do as follows.")
  BiosDocHelp_L("")
  BiosDocHelp_L("CALL 017AH  ; Write current reset status into A register.")
  BiosDocHelp_L("OR   80H    ; Set reset flag.")
  BiosDocHelp_L("CALL 017DH  ; Write a new value.")
  BiosDocHelp_L("JP   0H     ; Jump to address 0.")
  BiosDocHelp_L("")
  BiosDocHelp_L("Note, there is no way to detect between software reset and hardware reset with MSX1 and MSX2.")
  BiosDocHelp_Commit("Reset", "Documentacao")

EndProcedure
